WEBVTT

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:05.639
Previously on Supernatural 22 years ago

00:00:05.674 --> 00:00:06.762
Sammy.

00:00:07.288 --> 00:00:09.185
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can.

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:10.098
Go!

00:00:10.133 --> 00:00:12.662
Their mother Mysteriously died

00:00:12.928 --> 00:00:15.110
Now two brothers...
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:15.145 --> 00:00:17.404
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:17.439 --> 00:00:19.664
Are on a quest to find their father

00:00:20.614 --> 00:00:21.652
This is dad's book.

00:00:21.687 --> 00:00:23.874
I think dad wants us to
pick up where he left off.

00:00:23.909 --> 00:00:25.933
You know, saving people. Hunting things.

00:00:25.968 --> 00:00:27.668
The family business.

00:00:27.831 --> 00:00:29.082
I got to find dad.

00:00:29.117 --> 00:00:31.666
That's the only thing I can think about.

00:00:50.491 --> 00:00:53.569
Where have you got those amp
up to? A hundred thousand volts.

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:56.383
Damn. Yeah, I want this raw
head extra freaking crispy.

00:00:56.419 --> 00:00:59.048
Now, remember you only get
one shot with these things.

00:00:59.531 --> 00:01:01.501
So make it count.

00:01:34.433 --> 00:01:35.462
On three.

00:01:36.339 --> 00:01:37.411
One.

00:01:37.902 --> 00:01:39.225
Two.

00:01:39.584 --> 00:01:40.944
Three.

00:01:44.636 --> 00:01:46.229
Is it still here?

00:01:46.264 --> 00:01:47.384
Okay.

00:01:47.419 --> 00:01:49.306
Okay, hold your sister's hand.
We're gonna get you out of here.

00:01:49.341 --> 00:01:50.980
Let's go, let's go.

00:01:54.462 --> 00:01:56.021
All right, go!

00:01:58.772 --> 00:02:00.230
Sam!

00:02:06.251 --> 00:02:08.058
Sam, get them out of here!

00:02:08.093 --> 00:02:09.443
Here, take this!

00:02:12.034 --> 00:02:13.836
Run!

00:02:20.884 --> 00:02:23.302
Come on!

00:03:01.764 --> 00:03:03.289
Dean!

00:03:04.069 --> 00:03:04.952
Dean!

00:03:05.173 --> 00:03:06.065
Hey!

00:03:06.504 --> 00:03:08.417
Hey, hey!

00:03:18.068 --> 00:03:19.605
Sorry, I'm so sorry to ask.

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:21.987
There doesn't seem to
be any insurance on file.

00:03:22.023 --> 00:03:24.038
Right, um...

00:03:25.756 --> 00:03:27.299
Okay.

00:03:28.764 --> 00:03:32.089
Okay, Mr. Burkevits.

00:03:34.572 --> 00:03:38.216
Look, we can finish this
up later. No, no it's okay.

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:41.235
We were just taking a short cut
through the neighborhood and um...

00:03:41.270 --> 00:03:44.033
Windows were all down,
we heard some screaming.

00:03:44.068 --> 00:03:46.797
We drove pass the house
and we stopped, ran in.

00:03:46.832 --> 00:03:48.333
And you found the kids in the basement.

00:03:48.369 --> 00:03:49.208
Yeah.

00:03:49.243 --> 00:03:51.498
Well, thank god you did.

00:03:51.909 --> 00:03:55.049
Excuse me. Sure, thanks for your help.

00:03:55.316 --> 00:03:56.265
Hey, doc. Is he...

00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:58.446
He's resting. And?

00:03:58.481 --> 00:04:00.981
The electrocution
triggered a heart attack.

00:04:01.016 --> 00:04:05.756
A pretty massive one. I'm
afraid his heart, it's damaged.

00:04:05.791 --> 00:04:08.444
How damaged? We've done all we can.

00:04:08.479 --> 00:04:11.714
We can try and keep him
comfortable at this point but...

00:04:11.749 --> 00:04:14.949
I'll give him a couple of
weeks at most, maybe a month.

00:04:14.985 --> 00:04:16.487
No, no, there is...

00:04:16.522 --> 00:04:19.379
There's gotta be something you
can do. Some kind of treatment.

00:04:19.414 --> 00:04:21.632
We can't work miracles.

00:04:21.667 --> 00:04:24.321
I really am sorry.

00:04:33.647 --> 00:04:39.287
You ever actually watched
daytime TV? It's terrible.

00:04:40.944 --> 00:04:42.535
I talked to your doctor.

00:04:42.571 --> 00:04:44.993
That fabric soft teddy bear, oh.

00:04:45.028 --> 00:04:47.914
I'll hunt that bitch down. Dean...

00:04:47.949 --> 00:04:50.171
Yeah.

00:04:50.206 --> 00:04:53.982
All right, well. Looks like
you're gonna leave town without me.

00:04:54.017 --> 00:04:56.055
What are you talking about?
I'm not gonna leave you here.

00:04:56.090 --> 00:04:57.968
Hey, if you take care of that car.

00:04:58.003 --> 00:04:59.811
I'll swear I'll hunt your ass.

00:04:59.846 --> 00:05:03.829
I don't think that's funny. Uh,
come on. It's a little funny.

00:05:10.947 --> 00:05:13.846
Look, Sam. What can I say,
man. It's a dangerous gig.

00:05:13.881 --> 00:05:16.304
I drew the short straw.
That it, end of story.

00:05:16.339 --> 00:05:18.591
Don't talk like that, all right?

00:05:18.626 --> 00:05:21.605
We still have options. What options?

00:05:21.640 --> 00:05:24.515
Get burial or cremation?

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:27.389
I know it's not easy.

00:05:28.542 --> 00:05:31.175
But I'm gonna die.

00:05:31.356 --> 00:05:34.101
And you can't stop it.

00:05:36.102 --> 00:05:37.850
Watch me.

00:05:37.885 --> 00:05:40.359
This is John Winchester.
I can't be reached.

00:05:40.394 --> 00:05:42.833
If this is an emergency
call my son Dean.

00:05:42.868 --> 00:05:48.157
866-907-3235.
He can help.

00:05:48.192 --> 00:05:50.940
Hey, dad. It's Sam.

00:05:52.216 --> 00:05:54.591
You probably won't get this but uh...

00:05:54.627 --> 00:05:56.552
It's Dean...

00:05:56.587 --> 00:05:59.302
He's sick and uh...

00:05:59.467 --> 00:06:03.102
Doctors says there
nothing they can do. Um...

00:06:04.393 --> 00:06:05.785
But uh...

00:06:05.820 --> 00:06:08.815
They don't know things
we know, right? Um...

00:06:08.850 --> 00:06:11.490
So, don't worry, cause I'm uh...

00:06:11.525 --> 00:06:14.626
Gonna do everything it
takes to get him better.

00:06:15.546 --> 00:06:17.030
All right.

00:06:17.065 --> 00:06:19.447
Just wanted you to know.

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:35.454
What the hell are you doing here?

00:06:35.489 --> 00:06:38.473
I checked myself out. Are you crazy?

00:06:38.508 --> 00:06:42.568
I'm not gonna die in a hospital
where the nurses aren't even hot.

00:06:42.812 --> 00:06:45.089
You know, this whole...

00:06:45.124 --> 00:06:47.565
I laugh in the face of
death thing... It's crap.

00:06:47.601 --> 00:06:49.900
I can see right through it.

00:06:49.935 --> 00:06:51.867
Yeah, whatever dude.

00:06:51.902 --> 00:06:54.107
Have you even slept?
You look worse than me.

00:06:54.142 --> 00:06:57.893
I've been scattering the
internet for the last three days.

00:06:59.476 --> 00:07:02.531
Calling every contact
in dad journal. For what?

00:07:02.566 --> 00:07:04.366
For what'll help you.

00:07:04.402 --> 00:07:07.470
One of dad's friends
Joshua. He called me back.

00:07:07.505 --> 00:07:10.052
Told me about a guy in
Nebraska. Specialist.

00:07:10.087 --> 00:07:12.599
You're not gonna let me
die in peace, are you?

00:07:12.634 --> 00:07:14.660
I'm not gonna let you die, period.

00:07:14.696 --> 00:07:17.190
We're going.

00:07:37.415 --> 00:07:40.545
The church of Roy Le Grange
Faith Healer. Witness the miracle

00:07:41.853 --> 00:07:44.819
I got you. I got it!

00:07:45.747 --> 00:07:47.687
Man, you're a lying bastard.

00:07:47.722 --> 00:07:49.794
I thought you said we
were going to see a doctor.

00:07:49.830 --> 00:07:51.524
I believe I said a 'specialist'.

00:07:51.559 --> 00:07:53.807
Look Dean, this guy's
suppose to be the real deal.

00:07:53.843 --> 00:07:57.291
I can't believe you brought me here to see
some guy who heals people out of a tent!

00:07:57.326 --> 00:08:00.317
Reverend Le Grange is a
great man. Yeah, that's nice.

00:08:00.352 --> 00:08:02.581
I have a right to protest.
This man is a fraud.

00:08:02.617 --> 00:08:05.074
He's bilking all these people
out of their hard earned money!

00:08:05.109 --> 00:08:08.527
This is a place of
worship. Let's go, move it.

00:08:08.562 --> 00:08:10.778
I take it he's not part of the flock.

00:08:10.813 --> 00:08:13.209
What would people see something
that they can't explain.

00:08:13.244 --> 00:08:15.605
There's controversy. Come
on, Sam. A Faith Healer?

00:08:15.640 --> 00:08:18.969
Maybe it's time to have
a little faith Dean.

00:08:19.725 --> 00:08:21.800
You know what I got faith in? Reality.

00:08:21.835 --> 00:08:24.042
Knowing what's really going on.

00:08:24.077 --> 00:08:25.630
How can you be a skeptic?

00:08:25.665 --> 00:08:27.098
With the things we see everyday.

00:08:27.133 --> 00:08:29.117
Exactly, we see them.
We know they're real.

00:08:29.152 --> 00:08:30.420
But if you know evil's out there

00:08:30.455 --> 00:08:32.028
How can you not believe
good's out there too?

00:08:32.063 --> 00:08:33.600
Cause I've seen what
evil does to good people.

00:08:33.635 --> 00:08:36.432
Maybe god works in mysterious ways.

00:08:36.995 --> 00:08:39.086
Maybe he does.

00:08:39.121 --> 00:08:41.410
I think you just turned
me Around on the subject.

00:08:41.445 --> 00:08:43.502
Yeah, I'm sure.

00:08:43.538 --> 00:08:45.639
I'm Dean. This is Sam.

00:08:45.674 --> 00:08:47.418
Leila.

00:08:47.453 --> 00:08:50.828
Sir, if you're not a believer
then why are you here?

00:08:50.863 --> 00:08:54.353
Well, apparently my brother here
believes enough for the both of us.

00:08:54.388 --> 00:08:57.656
Come on Leila. It's
about to start. All right.

00:08:57.691 --> 00:08:59.433
Bye.

00:08:59.701 --> 00:09:02.663
Well, I bet you, she can
work in mysterious ways.

00:09:02.698 --> 00:09:04.799
Ladies and gentlemen, please be seated.

00:09:04.834 --> 00:09:08.141
We're starting in just a moment.
Welcome all faiths True believers revival

00:09:10.465 --> 00:09:13.780
Yeah, peace love and trust all over.

00:09:18.463 --> 00:09:19.519
Come on.

00:09:19.554 --> 00:09:20.863
Don't, we're sitting here.

00:09:20.898 --> 00:09:22.306
We're sitting up front.

00:09:22.341 --> 00:09:23.714
What? Why? Come on.

00:09:23.749 --> 00:09:25.247
Oh, come on Sam.

00:09:25.282 --> 00:09:26.710
You're all right?

00:09:26.745 --> 00:09:30.426
This is ridiculous. I'm
good, dude. Get off me.

00:09:31.457 --> 00:09:33.448
Perfect. Yeah, perfect.

00:09:33.484 --> 00:09:35.424
Take it off

00:09:45.185 --> 00:09:49.806
Each morning my wife Sue
Ann brings me the news.

00:09:49.841 --> 00:09:52.367
Never seems good, does it? No.

00:09:52.402 --> 00:09:54.859
Seems like there's always someone

00:09:54.894 --> 00:10:00.322
Committing some immoral,
unspeakable act. That's right.

00:10:00.358 --> 00:10:03.461
But I say to you. God is watching.

00:10:03.496 --> 00:10:04.912
Here, here.

00:10:04.947 --> 00:10:11.491
God rewards the good and he
punishes the corrupt. Right.

00:10:11.526 --> 00:10:16.136
It is the Lord who does
the healing here friends.

00:10:16.172 --> 00:10:20.713
The Lord who guides me
and chosen who to heal

00:10:20.748 --> 00:10:24.343
By helping me to see into
people's hearts. Amen.

00:10:24.378 --> 00:10:26.798
Yeah, rid of their wallets.

00:10:26.833 --> 00:10:29.218
You think so young man?

00:10:30.664 --> 00:10:34.097
Sorry. No, no. Don't be.

00:10:34.132 --> 00:10:39.093
Just watch what you say around a
blind man. We got real sharp ears.

00:10:40.153 --> 00:10:42.557
What's your name son?

00:10:43.197 --> 00:10:45.983
Dean. Dean.

00:10:47.731 --> 00:10:51.534
I want you to come up here with me.

00:10:58.521 --> 00:11:01.104
No, it's okay.

00:11:01.292 --> 00:11:02.397
What are you doing?

00:11:02.432 --> 00:11:06.340
You come here to be healed, haven't you?

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:11.390
Oh, yeah but uh...

00:11:11.425 --> 00:11:15.381
Maybe you should just pick someone else.

00:11:17.891 --> 00:11:22.530
I didn't pick you Dean. The Lord did.

00:11:24.017 --> 00:11:26.424
Get up there!

00:11:26.654 --> 00:11:30.814
Yes. Yes. Amen.

00:11:37.081 --> 00:11:38.814
You're ready?

00:11:38.849 --> 00:11:41.663
Yeah, with no disrespect but uh...

00:11:41.698 --> 00:11:44.497
I'm not exactly a believer.

00:11:44.643 --> 00:11:46.536
You will be son.

00:11:46.571 --> 00:11:48.428
You will be.

00:11:48.613 --> 00:11:51.298
Pray with me friends.

00:12:15.064 --> 00:12:19.273
All right now.

00:12:28.307 --> 00:12:30.921
All right now.

00:12:35.388 --> 00:12:37.112
Dean!

00:12:41.989 --> 00:12:44.037
Say something!

00:12:57.421 --> 00:12:59.283
So you really feel okay?

00:12:59.319 --> 00:13:00.642
I feel fine Sam.

00:13:00.677 --> 00:13:04.554
Well, according to all your tests.
There's nothing wrong with your heart.

00:13:04.590 --> 00:13:06.321
No sign there ever was.

00:13:06.357 --> 00:13:10.104
Not that a man your age should
be having heart trouble but uh...

00:13:10.139 --> 00:13:12.126
Still it's strange, it does happen.

00:13:12.161 --> 00:13:13.291
What do you mean strange?

00:13:13.326 --> 00:13:16.954
Well, just yesterday a young
guy like you. 27, athletic.

00:13:16.989 --> 00:13:19.668
I don't know a heart attack.

00:13:20.512 --> 00:13:22.317
Thanks doc.

00:13:22.352 --> 00:13:24.122
No problem.

00:13:25.282 --> 00:13:27.396
That's odd. Maybe it's coincidence.

00:13:27.432 --> 00:13:29.560
People's heart give up all
the time, man. No they don't.

00:13:29.595 --> 00:13:31.653
Look Dean. Do we really have
to look this one in the mouth?

00:13:31.689 --> 00:13:34.333
Why can't we just be thankful that
the guy saved your life and move on?

00:13:34.368 --> 00:13:37.110
Because I can't shake
this feeling, that's why.

00:13:37.145 --> 00:13:39.070
What feeling?

00:13:39.105 --> 00:13:42.549
When I was healed. I just, I felt wrong.

00:13:42.584 --> 00:13:45.868
Felt cold and for a second

00:13:45.903 --> 00:13:47.795
I saw someone. I saw this old man.

00:13:47.830 --> 00:13:49.651
I'm telling you Sam. It was a spirit.

00:13:49.686 --> 00:13:52.306
But if there was something there
Dean. I think I would have seen it too.

00:13:52.341 --> 00:13:54.543
I mean I've been seeing
awful lot of things lately.

00:13:54.578 --> 00:13:56.299
Well, excuse me psychic wonder.

00:13:56.334 --> 00:13:59.276
But you just need a
little faith on this one.

00:13:59.312 --> 00:14:03.470
Sam, I've been hunting long enough
to trust a feeling like this.

00:14:05.784 --> 00:14:07.779
Yeah, right.

00:14:08.856 --> 00:14:11.108
So what do you want to do?

00:14:11.143 --> 00:14:12.525
Why don't you to check
out that heart attack guy.

00:14:12.560 --> 00:14:14.765
I'm gonna visit the reverend.

00:14:17.706 --> 00:14:19.305
I feel great.

00:14:19.340 --> 00:14:20.869
Just trying to...

00:14:20.905 --> 00:14:22.994
You know, make sense of what happened.

00:14:23.029 --> 00:14:25.933
A miracle's what happened.

00:14:26.313 --> 00:14:30.858
Miracles come so often around Roy.

00:14:31.554 --> 00:14:34.173
When did they start? The miracles.

00:14:34.209 --> 00:14:36.758
Woke up one morning stone blind.

00:14:36.793 --> 00:14:41.142
Doctors figured out I had cancer.
Told me I had maybe a month.

00:14:41.177 --> 00:14:42.742
So uh...

00:14:42.777 --> 00:14:45.042
We prayed for a miracle.

00:14:45.077 --> 00:14:47.667
I was weak but...

00:14:47.702 --> 00:14:51.110
I told Sue Ann to just keep on praying.

00:14:51.145 --> 00:14:52.688
I went into a coma.

00:14:52.723 --> 00:14:55.534
Doctors said I wouldn't
wake up but I did.

00:14:55.569 --> 00:14:58.044
And the cancer was gone.

00:14:58.079 --> 00:15:03.763
If it wasn't for these eyes, no
one would believe I ever had it.

00:15:03.799 --> 00:15:06.483
And suddenly you can heal people?

00:15:06.518 --> 00:15:09.102
I discovered it afterwards, yes.

00:15:09.137 --> 00:15:11.650
God's blessed me in many ways.

00:15:11.685 --> 00:15:17.242
And his flock swelled over night.
And this is just the beginning.

00:15:18.885 --> 00:15:21.109
Can I ask you one last question?

00:15:21.145 --> 00:15:23.388
Of course you can.

00:15:24.082 --> 00:15:26.653
Why? Why me?

00:15:26.688 --> 00:15:30.052
Out of all the sick people why save me?

00:15:30.087 --> 00:15:33.878
Well, like I said before.
The Lord guides me.

00:15:33.914 --> 00:15:41.359
I looked into your heart and you
just stood out from all the rest.

00:15:41.524 --> 00:15:45.165
What did you see in my heart?

00:15:45.200 --> 00:15:48.975
A young man with an important
purpose. A job to do.

00:15:49.010 --> 00:15:52.044
And it isn't finished.

00:15:53.776 --> 00:15:57.887
He seemed healthy. Swam
everyday. Didn't smoke.

00:15:57.922 --> 00:16:00.795
It's no so hard to act this
kind of scene. No bizarre.

00:16:00.830 --> 00:16:03.667
And you said he was running?
Right before he collapsed?

00:16:03.702 --> 00:16:05.587
Yeah, yeah. He was freaking out.

00:16:05.622 --> 00:16:07.340
Said that something was...

00:16:07.375 --> 00:16:09.023
After him. Did he say what?

00:16:09.059 --> 00:16:12.726
Thin air, that's what. I
mean, there wasn't anything.

00:16:12.911 --> 00:16:14.805
All right, thanks.

00:16:17.270 --> 00:16:18.750
Hey buddy. You're...

00:16:18.785 --> 00:16:20.264
You're clock's busted.

00:16:20.299 --> 00:16:21.709
Oh, yeah. We uh...

00:16:21.744 --> 00:16:26.233
We can't get it working.
Just froze at 4:17.

00:16:26.268 --> 00:16:28.846
Is that the same time Marshall died?

00:16:28.881 --> 00:16:30.746
How did you know?

00:16:34.238 --> 00:16:36.795
Dean, hey. Hey.

00:16:36.993 --> 00:16:38.706
How you feeling? I feel good.

00:16:38.741 --> 00:16:41.147
Cured, I guess.

00:16:41.183 --> 00:16:42.752
What are you doing here?

00:16:42.787 --> 00:16:46.029
You know my mom. She wanted
to talk to the reverend.

00:16:46.064 --> 00:16:47.787
Leila.

00:16:48.825 --> 00:16:52.961
Yes, we're here again. Oh,
I'm sorry but Roy's resting.

00:16:52.997 --> 00:16:55.397
He won't be seeing anyone right now.

00:16:55.432 --> 00:16:57.441
Sue Ann please.

00:16:57.476 --> 00:17:00.130
This is our sixth time.
He's got to see us.

00:17:00.165 --> 00:17:02.354
Roy is aware of Leila's situation

00:17:02.389 --> 00:17:05.520
And he very well much wants to help
just as soon as the Lord allows.

00:17:05.556 --> 00:17:08.861
Have faith Mrs. Roke.

00:17:17.110 --> 00:17:18.619
Why are you still even here?

00:17:18.654 --> 00:17:20.716
You've got what you wanted. Mom.

00:17:20.751 --> 00:17:22.586
Stop.

00:17:22.622 --> 00:17:25.208
No Leila this is too much.

00:17:25.243 --> 00:17:27.733
We've been to every single service.

00:17:27.768 --> 00:17:30.695
If Roy would stop choosing
these strangers over you.

00:17:30.730 --> 00:17:33.906
Strangers who don't even believe.

00:17:33.941 --> 00:17:37.081
I just can't pray any harder.

00:17:37.116 --> 00:17:39.738
Leila, what's wrong?

00:17:41.951 --> 00:17:44.252
I have this thing.

00:17:44.287 --> 00:17:46.553
It's a brain tumor.

00:17:47.010 --> 00:17:49.967
It's inoperable.

00:17:50.143 --> 00:17:53.893
In sixth months the doctors say...

00:17:58.346 --> 00:18:00.590
I'm sorry.

00:18:01.126 --> 00:18:03.034
It's okay.

00:18:03.069 --> 00:18:05.057
No.

00:18:05.344 --> 00:18:08.070
It isn't.

00:18:13.288 --> 00:18:17.719
Why do you deserve to
live more than my daughter?

00:18:46.207 --> 00:18:48.555
What did you find out?

00:18:49.186 --> 00:18:51.206
I'm sorry.

00:18:51.394 --> 00:18:52.590
Sorry about what?

00:18:52.625 --> 00:18:58.181
Marshall Hall died at 4:17.

00:18:58.400 --> 00:19:00.898
The exact time I was healed. Yeah.

00:19:00.933 --> 00:19:04.490
So, I put together a list.
Everyone Roy's healed.

00:19:04.526 --> 00:19:08.151
Six people over the past year and I
cross checked them with local obits.

00:19:08.186 --> 00:19:10.898
Every time someone was
healed someone else died.

00:19:10.933 --> 00:19:12.325
And each time the victim died

00:19:12.360 --> 00:19:15.242
Of the same symptom Le Grange
was healing at the time.

00:19:15.277 --> 00:19:18.125
Someone healed a cancer,
someone else died of cancer?

00:19:18.160 --> 00:19:21.544
Somehow. Le Grange...

00:19:21.729 --> 00:19:25.939
Is trading a life for another. Hello?

00:19:27.115 --> 00:19:28.825
Wait, wait, wait. So...

00:19:28.861 --> 00:19:31.448
Marshall Hall died to save me?

00:19:31.483 --> 00:19:33.385
Dean...

00:19:33.599 --> 00:19:36.035
The guy probably would have died anyway.

00:19:36.070 --> 00:19:38.471
And someone else would have been healed.

00:19:40.633 --> 00:19:43.011
You never should have brought me here.

00:19:43.046 --> 00:19:45.605
Dean, I was just trying
to save your life.

00:19:45.640 --> 00:19:48.164
But Sam, some guy is
dead now because of me!

00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:50.985
I didn't know.

00:19:51.824 --> 00:19:54.843
Pray with me friends.

00:19:55.688 --> 00:19:58.890
The thing I don't understand
is how is Roy doing it?

00:19:58.925 --> 00:20:01.748
How's he trading a life for a life?

00:20:01.783 --> 00:20:04.541
Oh, he's not doing it.

00:20:04.686 --> 00:20:06.825
Something else is doing it for him.

00:20:06.860 --> 00:20:11.161
What do you mean? The
old man I saw on stage.

00:20:11.553 --> 00:20:13.358
I didn't want to believe
it. But deep down, I knew it.

00:20:13.393 --> 00:20:15.459
You knew what? What
are you talking about?

00:20:15.494 --> 00:20:19.874
There's only one thing that can
give and take life like that.

00:20:19.909 --> 00:20:22.551
We're dealing with a reaper.

00:21:22.699 --> 00:21:24.467
You really think it's the 'Grim Reaper'?

00:21:24.502 --> 00:21:27.500
Like Angel of Death, the
Collector of Soul the whole deal?

00:21:27.535 --> 00:21:30.036
No, no, no. Not 'The
Reaper'. A 'Reaper'.

00:21:30.071 --> 00:21:32.397
There's reaper law in pretty
much every culture on earth.

00:21:32.432 --> 00:21:34.173
They go by a hundred different names.

00:21:34.208 --> 00:21:36.164
It's possible this one's one of them.

00:21:36.199 --> 00:21:38.084
But you said you saw a dude in a suit.

00:21:38.120 --> 00:21:42.100
What? You think he should be
working the whole black robe thing?

00:21:42.136 --> 00:21:44.998
You said it yourself that
the clock stopped right?

00:21:45.906 --> 00:21:47.948
Reapers stop time.

00:21:47.983 --> 00:21:49.475
And you can only see them
when they're coming at you

00:21:49.510 --> 00:21:51.540
Which is why I could
see him and you couldn't.

00:21:51.575 --> 00:21:53.535
Maybe. There's nothing
else that could be Sam.

00:21:53.570 --> 00:21:56.813
The question is how's Roy
controlling the damn thing.

00:21:56.848 --> 00:21:58.511
That cross.

00:21:58.546 --> 00:22:00.954
What? There was this cross.

00:22:00.990 --> 00:22:05.585
I noticed it in the church
tent, I knew I seen it before.

00:22:11.333 --> 00:22:13.191
Here.

00:22:13.737 --> 00:22:14.847
Tarot?

00:22:14.882 --> 00:22:16.438
It makes sense.

00:22:16.473 --> 00:22:18.633
I mean, tarot dates back to
the early Christian, right?

00:22:18.668 --> 00:22:20.406
When some priests
were still using magic?

00:22:20.441 --> 00:22:22.109
And a few of them viewed
into the dark stuff.

00:22:22.144 --> 00:22:26.337
Necromancy and how to push
death away, how to cause it.

00:22:26.372 --> 00:22:29.234
So Roy's using black
magic to bind the reaper.

00:22:29.269 --> 00:22:31.438
If he is, he's riding the whirlwind.

00:22:31.473 --> 00:22:35.410
It's like putting a dog
leash on a great white.

00:22:41.575 --> 00:22:44.329
Okay, then we stop Roy. How?

00:22:44.364 --> 00:22:45.338
You know how?

00:22:45.373 --> 00:22:46.778
Wait, what the hell are
you talking about Dean?

00:22:46.813 --> 00:22:48.633
We can't kill Roy.

00:22:48.669 --> 00:22:49.826
Sam. The guy's playing god.

00:22:49.861 --> 00:22:52.489
He's deciding who lives and who
dies. That's a monster in my books.

00:22:52.524 --> 00:22:55.400
No, we're not gonna
kill a human being Dean.

00:22:55.436 --> 00:22:57.337
We do that, we're no better than he is.

00:22:57.372 --> 00:23:00.167
Okay, so we can't kill
Roy. We can't kill death.

00:23:00.203 --> 00:23:03.263
Any bright ideas college boy?

00:23:03.555 --> 00:23:04.891
Okay, uh...

00:23:04.926 --> 00:23:07.316
If Roy's using some kind
of black spell on the reaper

00:23:07.351 --> 00:23:09.754
We gotta figure out what it is.

00:23:09.789 --> 00:23:12.328
And how to break it.

00:23:17.434 --> 00:23:20.673
Service today.

00:23:25.444 --> 00:23:28.093
If Roy's using a spell.
There might be a spell book.

00:23:28.128 --> 00:23:29.299
See if you can find it.

00:23:29.335 --> 00:23:32.175
Hurry up. Services start in 15
minutes. I'll try to stroll Roy.

00:23:32.210 --> 00:23:34.964
All right. Le Grange is
a fraud. He's no healer.

00:23:34.999 --> 00:23:36.673
Amen, brother. You
keep up the good work.

00:23:36.708 --> 00:23:38.369
Thank you.

00:24:35.424 --> 00:24:37.725
Encyclopedia of Christian
History Old & New Testament

00:25:04.395 --> 00:25:10.018
Openly gay teacher wins lawsuit
Strong message sent to Nations...

00:25:20.182 --> 00:25:23.453
Wright: 'local church a cult'

00:25:33.018 --> 00:25:33.905
What have you got?

00:25:33.940 --> 00:25:35.938
Roy's choosing victims
he sees as a immoral.

00:25:35.973 --> 00:25:37.901
And I think I know
who's next on his list.

00:25:37.936 --> 00:25:39.958
Remember the protestor?
The guy in the parking lot?

00:25:39.993 --> 00:25:42.025
Yeah. Yeah, I'll find him.

00:25:42.060 --> 00:25:45.018
But you can't let Roy
heal anyone, all right?

00:26:05.716 --> 00:26:06.655
Leila.

00:26:06.691 --> 00:26:09.928
Leila Roke, come up here child.

00:26:15.240 --> 00:26:17.250
Mom... Baby.

00:26:17.285 --> 00:26:19.260
I love you.

00:26:20.314 --> 00:26:22.414
Oh, man.

00:26:31.578 --> 00:26:34.265
Leila, listen to me.
You can't get up there.

00:26:34.301 --> 00:26:36.251
Why not? We've waited for months.

00:26:36.286 --> 00:26:38.057
You can't let Roy heal you.

00:26:38.093 --> 00:26:40.114
I don't understand. Roy
healed you, didn't he?

00:26:40.149 --> 00:26:42.100
I mean, why wouldn't
you at least let him try?

00:26:42.135 --> 00:26:45.354
Because if you do, something
bad is going to happen.

00:26:45.389 --> 00:26:48.572
I can't explain. I just need
you to believe me. Leila.

00:26:48.608 --> 00:26:50.780
Please...

00:26:59.078 --> 00:27:00.496
I'm sorry.

00:27:00.531 --> 00:27:02.406
Leila. Leila!

00:27:02.442 --> 00:27:04.282
Dear child.

00:27:05.377 --> 00:27:08.575
You deserve this. I knew
the Lord would reply me...

00:27:08.610 --> 00:27:11.520
I knew the Lord would reply me.

00:27:15.003 --> 00:27:16.875
Help!

00:27:23.983 --> 00:27:26.344
Pray with me friends.

00:27:30.447 --> 00:27:33.545
I hope you're ready. I am.

00:27:43.862 --> 00:27:45.208
Help!

00:27:45.243 --> 00:27:46.607
Help me please!

00:27:46.642 --> 00:27:47.970
Where is it?

00:27:48.186 --> 00:27:50.447
It's right there!

00:27:51.886 --> 00:27:53.906
Come on, come on.

00:28:02.692 --> 00:28:04.168
Fire!

00:28:04.203 --> 00:28:06.784
The tent's on fire!

00:28:06.933 --> 00:28:08.928
Fire! Everybody get out of here!

00:28:08.963 --> 00:28:11.523
Roy! Roy, please!

00:28:11.558 --> 00:28:13.679
Please don't stop. Please!

00:28:13.715 --> 00:28:15.663
Reverend, please!

00:28:15.698 --> 00:28:17.612
Please don't stop.

00:28:17.647 --> 00:28:19.238
Please.

00:28:19.273 --> 00:28:20.794
Friends.

00:28:20.829 --> 00:28:24.419
If you all just leave the tent
in an orderly fashion and...

00:28:24.454 --> 00:28:27.138
We'll figure out what's
going on out there and...

00:28:27.173 --> 00:28:30.042
I did it. I stopped Roy.

00:28:30.077 --> 00:28:32.910
David? I think its okay.

00:28:36.675 --> 00:28:38.292
No!

00:28:38.327 --> 00:28:39.523
Dean, it didn't work!

00:28:39.559 --> 00:28:41.553
The reaper's still coming!

00:28:42.530 --> 00:28:44.080
I'm telling you... I'm telling you.

00:28:44.115 --> 00:28:46.724
It must not have worked! Roy must
not be controlling this thing!

00:28:46.759 --> 00:28:49.262
Then who the hell is?

00:28:52.325 --> 00:28:54.447
Sue Ann.

00:29:08.645 --> 00:29:10.947
Help! Help me!

00:29:11.091 --> 00:29:12.888
Help!

00:29:27.377 --> 00:29:29.709
I got you. I got you.

00:29:32.263 --> 00:29:34.254
Thank god.

00:29:39.556 --> 00:29:42.603
I just don't understand.

00:29:42.638 --> 00:29:44.408
After everything we have done for you.

00:29:44.443 --> 00:29:47.547
After Roy healed you.

00:29:48.505 --> 00:29:52.869
I'm just very very disappointed Dean.

00:29:54.210 --> 00:29:56.693
You can let him go. I'm
not gonna press charges.

00:29:56.728 --> 00:30:01.903
The Lord will deal
with him as he sees fit.

00:30:03.655 --> 00:30:05.236
We catch you around here again son.

00:30:05.271 --> 00:30:07.998
Who put the fear god in you, understand?

00:30:08.033 --> 00:30:09.772
Yes, sir. Fear god.

00:30:09.807 --> 00:30:11.633
Got it.

00:30:14.698 --> 00:30:16.236
Leila.

00:30:16.927 --> 00:30:18.557
Why would you do that Dean?

00:30:18.592 --> 00:30:20.896
It could have been my only chance.

00:30:20.931 --> 00:30:22.881
He's not a healer.

00:30:22.916 --> 00:30:24.831
He healed you.

00:30:26.476 --> 00:30:28.527
I know it doesn't seem fair.

00:30:28.562 --> 00:30:33.179
And I wish I could explain. But
Roy's not the answer, I'm sorry.

00:30:35.166 --> 00:30:37.682
Goodbye Dean.

00:30:42.277 --> 00:30:46.262
I wish you luck. I really do.

00:30:46.297 --> 00:30:48.885
Same to you.

00:30:52.877 --> 00:30:56.184
You deserve it a lot more than me.

00:30:59.550 --> 00:31:02.025
Private session tonight.
No interruptions.

00:31:02.060 --> 00:31:04.500
I give you my word.
I'll heal your daughter.

00:31:04.535 --> 00:31:08.040
Thank you, reverend. God bless you.

00:31:12.167 --> 00:31:15.453
So Roy really believes.

00:31:15.994 --> 00:31:18.653
I don't think he has any
idea what his wife's doing.

00:31:18.689 --> 00:31:22.877
Well, I found this
Hidden in their library.

00:31:22.912 --> 00:31:26.186
It's ancient. Written by a
priest who went dark side.

00:31:26.222 --> 00:31:28.269
There's a binding spell in here.

00:31:28.304 --> 00:31:30.100
For trapping a reaper.

00:31:30.135 --> 00:31:32.497
Must be hell of a spell. Yeah.

00:31:32.532 --> 00:31:35.769
You got to build a black altar
with seriously dark stuff.

00:31:35.804 --> 00:31:39.272
Bones. Human blood.

00:31:39.307 --> 00:31:42.781
To cross a line like
that. That preacher's wife.

00:31:42.816 --> 00:31:47.343
Black magic, murder, evil.

00:31:47.378 --> 00:31:49.154
Desperate.

00:31:49.189 --> 00:31:52.475
Her husband was dying. She would
have done anything to save him.

00:31:52.510 --> 00:31:55.761
She was using the binding spell
to keep the reaper away from Roy.

00:31:55.796 --> 00:31:59.416
Cheating death. Literally.

00:31:59.451 --> 00:32:02.838
Yeah, but Roy's alive so why
is she still using the spell?

00:32:02.874 --> 00:32:08.402
Right. To force the reaper to help
the people she thinks are moral.

00:32:09.410 --> 00:32:12.884
Thank god save us from half the people
who think they're doing god's work.

00:32:12.920 --> 00:32:16.497
We got to break that binding spell Dean.

00:32:18.720 --> 00:32:21.126
You know Sue Ann had to
cop a cross like this.

00:32:21.161 --> 00:32:23.498
And when she dropped it
the reaper backed off.

00:32:23.533 --> 00:32:26.421
So you think we got to find
the cross or destroy the altar.

00:32:26.457 --> 00:32:28.408
Maybe both?

00:32:29.444 --> 00:32:31.869
Whatever we do. We'd
better to do it soon.

00:32:31.904 --> 00:32:34.877
Roy's healing Leila tonight.

00:32:46.769 --> 00:32:48.653
That's Leila's car.

00:32:48.688 --> 00:32:50.536
She's already here.

00:32:50.572 --> 00:32:52.331
Yeah.

00:32:53.095 --> 00:32:55.847
Dean. You know, if Roy would
have picked Leila instead of me.

00:32:55.882 --> 00:32:58.015
She'd be healed by now. Dean, don't.

00:32:58.050 --> 00:33:00.343
And if she's not healed tonight...

00:33:00.378 --> 00:33:02.780
She's gonna die in a couple of months.

00:33:02.815 --> 00:33:05.149
What's happening to her is horrible.

00:33:05.184 --> 00:33:09.512
But what are you going to do?
Let somebody else die to save her?

00:33:09.547 --> 00:33:14.196
You said it yourself
Dean. You can't play god.

00:33:28.102 --> 00:33:29.143
Gather around.

00:33:29.178 --> 00:33:31.340
Please, everyone gather around.

00:33:31.375 --> 00:33:33.502
Come in closer. Come on up.

00:33:33.537 --> 00:33:35.803
Where's Sue Ann?

00:33:36.230 --> 00:33:38.253
House.

00:33:39.068 --> 00:33:40.582
Go find Sue Ann. I'll catch up.

00:33:40.617 --> 00:33:42.105
What are you...

00:33:43.492 --> 00:33:45.149
Hey.

00:33:45.862 --> 00:33:49.251
You're gonna put that fear god in me?

00:34:33.078 --> 00:34:34.868
See him?

00:34:35.193 --> 00:34:37.035
Na.

00:34:58.088 --> 00:35:00.522
Psycho mutt.

00:35:46.051 --> 00:35:50.213
I gave your brother a life
and I can take it away.

00:36:01.813 --> 00:36:03.730
Sam, can't you see?

00:36:03.765 --> 00:36:05.613
The Lord chose me.

00:36:05.648 --> 00:36:08.394
The reward the just
and punish the wicked.

00:36:08.429 --> 00:36:10.786
And your brother is wicked.

00:36:10.821 --> 00:36:15.219
And he deserves to die just
as Leila deserves to live.

00:36:15.254 --> 00:36:17.964
That's god's will.

00:36:20.183 --> 00:36:22.712
Goodbye Sam.

00:36:26.794 --> 00:36:28.487
Mrs. Roke.

00:36:28.522 --> 00:36:30.705
You pray with me now.

00:36:30.740 --> 00:36:32.888
Pray with me friends.

00:37:02.146 --> 00:37:04.227
All right now.

00:37:05.294 --> 00:37:08.132
All right now.

00:37:33.975 --> 00:37:35.912
All right.

00:38:01.527 --> 00:38:06.765
I don't understand. I
don't feel different.

00:38:07.607 --> 00:38:08.681
My god!

00:38:08.716 --> 00:38:10.643
What have you done?

00:38:10.678 --> 00:38:12.569
He's not your god.

00:38:12.605 --> 00:38:14.617
Reverend?

00:38:14.652 --> 00:38:16.630
Sue Ann?

00:39:03.130 --> 00:39:04.854
You okay?

00:39:05.143 --> 00:39:07.220
A little bit weak.

00:39:07.255 --> 00:39:08.898
Yeah.

00:39:10.105 --> 00:39:11.972
All right, come on.

00:39:12.007 --> 00:39:13.840
We should get going.

00:39:25.231 --> 00:39:27.333
What is it?

00:39:27.368 --> 00:39:29.436
Nothing.

00:39:30.820 --> 00:39:32.103
What is it?

00:39:32.138 --> 00:39:34.076
We did the right thing here, didn't' we?

00:39:34.111 --> 00:39:36.152
Of course we did.

00:39:36.188 --> 00:39:38.519
I didn't feel like it.

00:39:39.621 --> 00:39:41.339
I got it.

00:39:45.180 --> 00:39:48.589
Leila, come on in. Hey.

00:39:48.624 --> 00:39:50.508
Hey.

00:39:51.357 --> 00:39:53.172
How did you know we were here?

00:39:53.207 --> 00:39:55.071
Sam called.

00:39:55.106 --> 00:39:58.867
He said you wanted to say goodbye.

00:39:59.035 --> 00:40:02.061
I'm gonna grab a soda.

00:40:06.800 --> 00:40:08.933
So um...

00:40:08.968 --> 00:40:12.162
Where are you going?

00:40:12.197 --> 00:40:13.373
Don't know yet.

00:40:13.408 --> 00:40:17.468
Our work kind of takes us all over so...

00:40:19.205 --> 00:40:23.586
You know, I went back to see Roy.

00:40:23.622 --> 00:40:26.261
What happened?

00:40:27.495 --> 00:40:29.816
Nothing.

00:40:30.039 --> 00:40:36.086
He laid his hand on my
forehead. But nothing happened.

00:40:36.121 --> 00:40:38.691
I'm sorry.

00:40:38.875 --> 00:40:41.465
I'm sorry it didn't work.

00:40:41.500 --> 00:40:43.445
And Sue Ann...

00:40:43.480 --> 00:40:45.151
She's dead, you know?

00:40:45.187 --> 00:40:47.109
A stroke.

00:40:47.144 --> 00:40:50.241
Yeah, I heard.

00:40:50.900 --> 00:40:54.055
Yeah, Roy's a good man.

00:40:54.229 --> 00:40:57.472
He doesn't deserve what's happened.

00:41:00.370 --> 00:41:02.724
Must be ruff...

00:41:02.760 --> 00:41:05.139
To believe in something so much.

00:41:05.174 --> 00:41:08.568
And have it disappoint you like that.

00:41:12.720 --> 00:41:16.035
You want to hear something weird?

00:41:17.241 --> 00:41:22.088
I'm okay. Really.

00:41:22.123 --> 00:41:24.491
I guess if you're gonna have faith

00:41:24.526 --> 00:41:27.682
We can't just have it
when the miracles happen.

00:41:27.717 --> 00:41:32.978
You have to have it when they don't.

00:41:37.647 --> 00:41:41.109
So what now?

00:41:43.531 --> 00:41:48.037
God works in mysterious ways.

00:41:52.183 --> 00:41:54.565
Goodbye Dean.

00:41:56.300 --> 00:41:58.023
Hey.

00:42:03.297 --> 00:42:08.410
I'm not much of a praying type but...

00:42:09.282 --> 00:42:12.769
I'm gonna pray for you.

00:42:13.932 --> 00:42:16.290
Well...

00:42:16.457 --> 00:42:19.956
There's a miracle right there.

00:00:03.582 --> 00:00:05.088
